1
00:00:00,002 --> 00:00:03,462
(Howard:)Bernadette, please, I'm asking you
to give me another chance.

2
00:00:03,755 --> 00:00:07,215
(Bernadette:)What do you think, Leonard?
Should I give him another chance?

3
00:00:07,384 --> 00:00:10,174
(Leonard:)It's up to you.
He didn't call your experiment stupid.

4
00:00:12,306 --> 00:00:13,556
Come here, tushy-face.

5
00:00:13,724 --> 00:00:15,394
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

6
00:00:15,601 --> 00:00:19,021
Tushy-face.
That is going on Twitter right now.

7
00:00:25,068 --> 00:00:27,568
(Bernadette:)Raj, you should've seen
Leonard's experiment.

8
00:00:27,738 --> 00:00:30,828
The interference pattern was cool
when the electron beam was on.

9
00:00:30,991 --> 00:00:35,161
(Leonard:)I'm glad you enjoyed it. Most people
aren't that interested in what I do.

10
00:00:40,125 --> 00:00:41,295
[CLEARS THROAT]

11
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:43,590
(Penny:)Actually, that's not true, Leonard.

12
00:00:43,754 --> 00:00:46,964
(Penny:)I've been thinking that, given
the parameters of your experiment...

13
00:00:47,132 --> 00:00:50,302
(Penny:)...the transport of electrons
through the nano-fabricated rings...

14
00:00:50,469 --> 00:00:54,889
...is no different than the experiment
already conducted in the Netherlands.

15
00:00:57,476 --> 00:01:00,936
(Penny:)Their observed phase shift in
the diffusing electrons inside the ring...

16
00:01:01,104 --> 00:01:03,274
...already demonstrated
the electric analogue...

17
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:06,280
(Leonard:)...of the Aharonov-Bohm
quantum interference effect.

18
00:01:11,865 --> 00:01:14,115
(Penny:)That's it. That's all I know.

19
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:16,410
(Penny:)Oh, wait.

20
00:01:17,371 --> 00:01:21,161
(Penny:)Fig Newtons were named after a town
in Massachusetts, not the scientist.

